3.2.m:
The king said:
"For my sake, a beautiful woman was prepared to surrender her own life;
what can be given to her by me, who am the object of that love?

Therefore, threefold action must indeed be performed here by adepts.
That twice-born performed the rite born of the mantra with another's wealth;
therefore, devoted to it, that twice-born attained the state of a yakṣa in another birth.”

The old brāhmaṇa said:
"He has manifold forms, is true to His promise, all-pervading, and stainless;
now He has come before your eyes in the form of a brāhmaṇa.

The sages said:
O blessed one, the ancient ones have declared the rite and conduct born of the hidden;
and among all votive observances, the votive observance of Nārāyaṇa is the best.

Therefore a wife should be taken by me in this dread Kali age;
if a woman should be mine who conforms to the disposition of my mind,
then my birth will be fruitful and my highest good will come to be here.”
